{"id":"396f9d3c403d0603","group":"89","path":"89/89-df-reflection-principle.md","title":"Reflection Principle","display":"df-reflection-principle — Reflection Principle","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"The Logic of Provability","book_abbrev":"89","label":"89-df-reflection-principle","aliases":["89-df-reflection-principle"],"display":"df-reflection-principle — Reflection Principle","depends_on":["[[89-df-provability-predicate]]","[[89-df-godel-numbering]]","[[89-df-numeral]]"],"revised":"2026-10-09"},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"The Logic of Provability"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"89"},{"key":"label","html":"89-df-reflection-principle"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>89-df-reflection-principle</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-reflection-principle — Reflection Principle"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"841985de31202f85\" href=\"?note=841985de31202f85\" title=\"89-df-provability-predicate\">89-df-provability-predicate</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"7f53d84c2164d9c5\" href=\"?note=7f53d84c2164d9c5\" title=\"89-df-godel-numbering\">89-df-godel-numbering</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"d088b00b91690ba0\" href=\"?note=d088b00b91690ba0\" title=\"89-df-numeral\">89-df-numeral</a></span></div>"},{"key":"revised","html":"2026-10-09"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_{T}\">\\(T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_{T}\\)</span> is a recursively axiomatized arithmetical theory.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Prov}_{T}(x)\">\\(\\mathrm{Prov}_{T}(x)\\)</span> is its fixed one-free-variable arithmetical provability formula.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\ulcorner\\cdot\\urcorner\">\\(\\ulcorner\\cdot\\urcorner\\)</span> is the fixed Gödel numbering and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\bar n\">\\(\\bar n\\)</span> is the numeral for <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"n\">\\(n\\)</span>.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}reflection\\text{-}principle}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{RFN}(T)\n\\coloneqq\n\\left\\{\n\\mathrm{Prov}_{T}(\\overline{\\ulcorner\\varphi\\urcorner})\\to\\varphi\n\\ \\middle|\\ \\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Sent}_{T}\n\\right\\}.\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}reflection\\text{-}principle}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{RFN}(T)\n\\coloneqq\n\\left\\{\n\\mathrm{Prov}_{T}(\\overline{\\ulcorner\\varphi\\urcorner})\\to\\varphi\n\\ \\middle|\\ \\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Sent}_{T}\n\\right\\}.\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<p>This is the <strong>local reflection schema</strong>, indexed externally by sentences; it is not\none object-language quantification over formula codes. Uniform reflection for\nformulas with free variables is a distinct, stronger schema.</p>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"89-df-provability-predicate","status":"resolved","id":"841985de31202f85","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[89-df-provability-predicate]]","embed":false},{"target":"89-df-godel-numbering","status":"resolved","id":"7f53d84c2164d9c5","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[89-df-godel-numbering]]","embed":false},{"target":"89-df-numeral","status":"resolved","id":"d088b00b91690ba0","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[89-df-numeral]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"T\\subseteq\\mathrm{Sent}_{T}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Prov}_{T}(x)","display":false},{"tex":"\\ulcorner\\cdot\\urcorner","display":false},{"tex":"\\bar n","display":false},{"tex":"n","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}reflection\\text{-}principle}\\vdash\n\\mathrm{RFN}(T)\n\\coloneqq\n\\left\\{\n\\mathrm{Prov}_{T}(\\overline{\\ulcorner\\varphi\\urcorner})\\to\\varphi\n\\ \\middle|\\ \\varphi\\in\\mathrm{Sent}_{T}\n\\right\\}.","display":true}],"bytes":1168,"backlinks":[{"id":"0d2469f2990d6f49","anchor":"ref-2","locations":["元数据 · depends_on"],"count":1,"excerpt":""},{"id":"1db7bc84524d0fdb","anchor":"ref-4","locations":["元数据 · depends_on","正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"reflection : 反射原则 (see [[89-df-reflection-principle]])"},{"id":"05a599f85e508061","anchor":"ref-26","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[89-df-reflection-principle]]"},{"id":"e0c421a5b45aeb77","anchor":"ref-60","locations":["正文"],"count":2,"excerpt":"[[89-df-arithmetical-interpretation]] → [[89-thm-generalized-diagonal-lemma]] → [[89-thm-lob-internal]] → [[89-thm-lob-theorem]] → [[89-df-reflection-principle]] → [[89-df-gls-logic]]"}],"outgoing":["841985de31202f85","7f53d84c2164d9c5","d088b00b91690ba0"]}